# Every message is one run. The FIRST message a page sends says what it wants
# bound to its socket: {"type":"connect"} for the display (/screen), or
# {"type":"attach","cols":C,"rows":R} for a terminal (/term). Parse it so the
# rules in scope 200 can read it. Once a socket is bound the chassis stops
# making runs for it — the frames go straight through — so this only ever
# sees that one message (and any sent after a detach).
WHEN @websocket.phase == "message" && @websocket.msg.text != ""
  EMIT .msg = &json(@websocket.msg.text)
